    {
      "id": "Fl1-Xd6m8Ceku3R1dOKOi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -439.70554871400566,
      "y": 24922.042127558274,
      "width": 715,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1552600855,
      "version": 42,
      "versionNonce": 1907474873,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1762614624450,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Session\nDefinition\nType: org.hibernate.Session (Interface)\nImplementation: SessionImpl (Class)\nPurpose: Main interface to communicate with the database\nCommunication Flow: Your Code → Session → JDBC API → SQL Database\nWhat is it?\nSession is an interface that:\n\nActs as a bridge between Java objects and database\nWraps JDBC Connection and communicates with database via JDBC\nLight-weight: Quick and cheap to create\nNOT thread-safe: Each thread needs its own Session instance\nShort-lived: Created per request/transaction, then closed\nFirst-level cache: Automatically caches entities during the\nsession\n\nHow it works:\nYour Code: session.persist(user)\n    ↓\nSession Interface (Hibernate)\n    ↓\nJDBC PreparedStatement/ResultSet\n    ↓\nSQL: INSERT INTO users VALUES (...)\n    ↓\nDatabase (MySQL/PostgreSQL)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Session\nDefinition\nType: org.hibernate.Session (Interface)\nImplementation: SessionImpl (Class)\nPurpose: Main interface to communicate with the database\nCommunication Flow: Your Code → Session → JDBC API → SQL Database\nWhat is it?\nSession is an interface that:\n\nActs as a bridge between Java objects and database\nWraps JDBC Connection and communicates with database via JDBC\nLight-weight: Quick and cheap to create\nNOT thread-safe: Each thread needs its own Session instance\nShort-lived: Created per request/transaction, then closed\nFirst-level cache: Automatically caches entities during the session\n\nHow it works:\nYour Code: session.persist(user)\n    ↓\nSession Interface (Hibernate)\n    ↓\nJDBC PreparedStatement/ResultSet\n    ↓\nSQL: INSERT INTO users VALUES (...)\n    ↓\nDatabase (MySQL/PostgreSQL)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
